# ####################################################################################
# # BARD NECRO ENHANCED
# ####################################################################################
# Replaces bard-necro and bard-necro-eval. Design, cooldown model and every barding
# number: blueprint/bard-necro-handbook.html (design in part 5, mechanics in part 2).
#
# Full loop: sustain, bard control, necro burst, spell opener and damage rotation.
#
# Needs
#   A shepherd's crook in the backpack only while config__use_herding is 1. It is 0: the
#   Herding slot went to Resisting Spells on 2026-09-27, so the crook does nothing.
#   Discordance, Peacemaking and Provocation all trained: the song round robin only moves
#   forward through a branch whose skill exists, so a missing one parks it.
#   An instrument in the backpack, a necromancer book, reagents for the spell table below.
#   Razor hotkeys, named exactly as Razor's hotkey list shows them:
#     agents      "> Smart Heal/Cure Self", "> Greater Heal/Cure Self", "> Interrupt"
#     potions     "Drink Heal", "Drink Cure", "Drink Refresh", "Drink Strength",
#                 "Drink Agility", "Drink Magic Resist", "Eat Magic Mushroom"
#     necromancy  "Blood Oath", "Corpse Skin", "Evil Omen", "Poison Strike",
#                 "Vampiric Embrace". They once looked broken and were swapped for the
#                 chat commands, [BloodOath and so on, but the real fault was a wrong
#                 ingump symbol count comparison.
#     targeting   "Target Self", "Cancel Current Target"
#   The hotbar's own Auto-Renew must be OFF for every ability this loop drives. It spends the
#   same symbols, and its priority is cheapest first, which is backwards for this build.
#
# Hotkey policy
#   Anything Razor exposes as a hotkey is driven through the hotkey, so one convention covers
#   potions, abilities and agents alike. findtype still answers "is there one to drink", it
#   just no longer does the drinking.
#   cooldowns.xml carries every bar this loop reads: music / song / disco / peace/provo,
#   the four proc entries magic arrow / harm / fireball / lightning, mush, heal pot, reflect
#   and walk. The names are lowercase and the glossary is blueprint/overheads.html.
#
# Naming convention
#   config__*  : tunable settings, kept at the top of the file
#   wait__*    : how long the script sleeps or waits for a target cursor
#   cooldown__*: thresholds compared against a timer__ or a named cooldown
#   var__*     : state owned by this script
#   alias__*   : result of an as binding from find / findtype
#   label__*   : result of getlabel
#   timer__*   : createtimer / settimer target
#   list__*    : createlist / pushlist target. A foreach loop variable carries no prefix
#   words are snake_case, the prefix is split off with a double underscore
#
# Literal policy
#   wait / waitfortarget / settimer / cooldown / comparison right-hand sides are lifted to
#   variables. find and findtype source / quantity and overhead hue stay numeric literals.
#   The engagement radius is the one deliberate exception: it is a tuning knob, so it lives
#   in config__target_range, the same way loadout.razor carries config__reach.
#
# Overhead policy
#   Every message is "[ subject, state ]" in lowercase, see blueprint/overheads.html for the words and the hue palette.
#     90  status and information, suppressed by config__chatty
#     53  warning, a resource is running out but the run continues
#     33  error, something is missing and the block cannot do its job
#     55  a prompt waiting on the player
#     118 / 83  a necro ability or a magery spell going out, subject only, the hue is the state
#   A resource problem leads with the noun so it reads at a glance. No exclamation marks.
#
# System message buffer
#   Nothing clears the buffer once the loop is running. The only clearsysmsg sits in the
#   setup above the loop. Clearing mid loop wipes lines other blocks still need, which is
#   exactly how the throwing script lost its planted readout.
#   The drain at the top of the loop catches a prompt left over from a previous pass. Each
#   useskill also answers the prompt inline, because that is where it normally appears.
#
# Action guards
#   casting, cooldown "walk" and targetexists are live server state, not facts a pass can
#   establish once. The drains at the top of the loop only prove they were clear when the
#   pass began: the player can start walking, open a cursor, or an earlier block can begin a
#   cast, all before a later block runs. So every block re-checks what applies to it.
#
#     a block that casts        not casting, cooldown "walk" = 0, not targetexists
#     a block that moves items  not casting, not targetexists
#     a block that only reads   nothing
#
#   cooldown "walk" is the manual control signal. While the player is steering, a cast would
#   either break on the step or fight the player for control, so casts stand down and item
#   use does not: drinking a potion while walking is fine, casting while walking is not.
#   casting is the opposite direction: our own spell in flight is what any other action
#   would interrupt, so everything that acts checks it.
#
# Manual mode
#   warmode on means the player is casting by hand. The loop's own casts and cursors, the
#   attacks, the bard skills, the self buffs, Create Food, and Corpse Skin and Evil Omen,
#   which only pay off through the loop's own spells, test not warmode on their gate line
#   and stand down, so nothing of ours lands on top of the player's cursor and the last
#   target they set stays theirs. What keeps the character alive keeps running, cures,
#   heals, potions and eating a mushroom, and so does Blood Oath, which pays off through
#   the followers. Turning warmode off hands the same target back to the loop. The bard
#   blocks read it together with the instrument: not warmode and var__instrument_ok = 1
#   and var__my_instrument != 0. Both used to be flags set on every pass, and reading
#   warmode where it is needed is five statements a pass less.
#
# Condition order
#   Every statement a pass steps on costs a tick, 5 to 20 ms here (blueprint/razor.html part 6),
#   and a gate that is nearly always true costs its tick for nothing. So in the hot path the
#   categories below share one line, the ones most often false first, and a block with
#   nothing to do costs a pass one statement:
#
#     1  var__ / config__ / skill / findbuff / counttype   what this script knows and wants
#     2  cooldown "..." / timer "..."                      what the game says is ready
#     3  not targetexists and not casting  [and Walk]      the act window
#     4  find / findtype ... as alias__                    the lookup the action consumes
#
#   The act window rides at the end of that line, read in the same tick as the rest, so it
#   is still read fresh, immediately before the action. The lookup stays on its own line
#   below, inside the arm that will act, so a pass that casts nothing never pays for it: the
#   opener and the proc core look their target up only once a spell is about to go.
#   var__engaged, the most selective test of all, is asked once, at COMBAT OR WALK, which
#   splits every pass into travel or combat so neither half steps through the other's blocks.
#
#   Checks that only need looking at now and then sit inside one five second HOUSEKEEPING
#   tick, each with its own longer clock inside where it has one, so a pass pays one
#   statement for all of them. Paralysis, poison and damage share one SURVIVAL test.
#
#   A label read only to learn that a state still holds is not read again on every pass:
#   DISCO skips a discorded target for thirty seconds, PEACE waits two seconds on a
#   pacified or broken one.
#
#   Blocks off the hot path, the setup, the reagent refresh and the like, keep one category
#   per line, where the nesting depth shows at a glance how many kinds of condition there are.
#
#   cooldown "walk" = 0 joins the act window only where the whole block casts. Where a
#   block mixes a drink with a cast it stays on the casting line, because drinking while
#   walking is fine and casting while walking is not.
#
#   A block driven by a while loop keeps its condition on the while line and takes the act
#   window immediately outside it, since nothing inside such a loop does anything but move
#   items.
#
# Targeted casts
#   A spell that takes a target spends its whole cast time before the cursor appears, so the
#   wait for the cursor IS the cast. Every targeted spell here takes the same shape:
#
#     cast 'X'
#     for 60                                  poll for the cursor instead of blocking on it
#         if targetexists           break     the cast finished
#         if disturbed              say, break the cast died and its cursor is never coming
#         if diffhits >= emergency  say, hotkey "> Interrupt", break
#                                             our own cast is the only thing standing
#                                             between the character and a heal
#         wait wait__poll
#     endfor
#
#   A fixed wait per circle would be shorter to write and it was considered. It loses on the
#   two things the poll is for: a cast disturbed at 0.1 seconds would still sit out the full
#   1.75, and hit points could not be looked at until the wait ended. The poll leaves within
#   100 ms of whichever comes first, and the per circle timing lives in the game, not here.
#     if targetexists
#         if dead alias__            cancel   it died during the cast
#         else target, wait wait__cast
#              if insysmsg "cannot be seen"   not delivered, record nothing
#              else                           record that it landed
#
#   Polling is the reference scripts' pattern and it is what makes the emergency interrupt
#   real. With a blocking waitfortarget the loop cannot look at hit points until the cursor
#   turns up, which for Energy Bolt is 1.75 seconds after the hit that mattered.
#
#   Casts that take no target, the heal agents, Create Food and the two self buffs, cannot be
#   polled for a cursor. They poll casting instead, bounded the same way. casting drops the
#   moment such a cast is disturbed, so the poll leaves on that and the disturb line is left
#   unread, as is the one an emergency interrupt brings in after its poll has already left.
#   A cursor poll that found such a line would take it for its own disturb, leave on its
#   first round, and strand its cursor. So the line is read off just before the first cursor
#   poll a pass can reach: ahead of the opener, and ahead of the Spell Siphon Magic Arrow.
#
#   The heal agents answer their own cursor only while there is something to heal. When the
#   hit points top up during the cast, a tamer's heal say, the cursor is left open, and every
#   block would stand down behind it. After each agent a cursor still open at full hit points
#   is cancelled.
#
#   Abilities on the necro hotbar are not spells: they resolve without a cursor and answer
#   with a message, so success is read from "unholy symbols remaining" rather than assumed.

clearall
clearsysmsg
cleardragdrop
clearignore

# ####################################################################################
# # CONFIG
# ####################################################################################
# Potions are consumables. Turn this off when farming somewhere that does not need them.
@setvar! config__use_potion 1

# 1 narrates what the script is doing, 0 keeps it quiet. Covers every 90 hue line: target
# changes, potions drunk, gold dropped, and every cast cut short for a heal, named by spell.
# A cast the server disturbs is not reported here: the profile's "[ cast, disturbed ]"
# overhead already says so, the script only consumes the line. Warnings and errors ignore
# this switch.
@setvar! config__chatty 1

# Magic instrument mode. 1 reads labels and holds out for a supremely or exceedingly
# prefix, 0 takes the first instrument found and skips getlabel entirely, which is the
# cheaper path when the shelf only stocks crafted instruments.
@setvar! config__use_magic_instrument 1

# 1 activates the shepherd's crook at startup. Herding is passive once a crook is set as
# the active one, and at Herding 80 it is worth 17.6% follower damage and 8.8% follower
# resistance against creatures, on the 63% of the damage the followers do. 0 while the
# skill slot is Resisting Spells instead: a crook without Herding does nothing.
@setvar! config__use_herding 0

# Self buffs kept up on the walk. Neither runs on a clock, both last until used up:
# Reactive Armor takes 20% off physical hits until 25 damage is prevented at Magery 100,
# Magic Reflection turns back the next hostile spell and then cannot be recast for 30
# seconds counted from the reflection, which the reflect bar tracks. 1 recasts each as soon as findbuff no
# longer sees it, so both are already up when the next pull, or a red, arrives. 0 leaves
# them to the Ctrl+Q / Ctrl+W keys.
@setvar! config__use_reactive_armor 1
@setvar! config__use_magic_reflect 1

# Fresh summons are renamed, in the order they appear, to lookalikes of the character's
# name, so a PK reading nameplates has to guess which of the four is the player. Each name
# is one slot: a resummon takes over the first name whose summon is gone. 0 leaves the
# stock names. config__summon_range is how far the block looks for summons, the whole
# screen, so a summon that lagged behind still holds its name.
# The names are a list, not variables: a script variable holds numbers and serials only,
# a word stored in one reads back as 4294967295, while a list entry keeps its text and
# foreach hands it to rename as it is. Digits are refused by the server, so a serial is
# not a name. Rebuilt on every start so an edit here is what the block reads.
@setvar! config__name_summons 1
@setvar! config__summon_range 18

if not listexists 'list__summon_names'
    createlist 'list__summon_names'
endif

clearlist 'list__summon_names'
pushlist 'list__summon_names' 'nomeehei'
pushlist 'list__summon_names' 'nomeehel'
pushlist 'list__summon_names' 'nomeeheh'

# How far a mob may be and still count as engaged. Everything that asks "am I fighting"
# goes through this one number, so the bard and spell stages inherit it unchanged.
@setvar! config__target_range 10

# How far the target the player picks is taken up from, the whole screen. The pets often
# open on a mob well past config__target_range, and a walk time song or self cast then
# overwrites lasttarget before that mob comes within reach. The loop keeps the target while
# it is on screen and only engages once it is inside config__target_range.
@setvar! config__acquire_range 18

# Damage taken, as hit points below maximum, that separates the cheap heal from the
# emergency path. The emergency figure is also what lets a cast in flight be cut short.
@setvar! config__light_hits 15
@setvar! config__emergency_hits 35

# 1 cancels a spell already in flight when damage crosses config__emergency_hits, 0 lets it
# finish. Goes through the "> Interrupt" hotkey, the same one the wheel is bound to.
@setvar! config__interrupt_to_heal 1

# How much gold one lift moves when shedding weight.
@setvar! config__gold_drop_amount 1000

# Mana a spell needs before it is worth starting, by circle. The rotation reads these
# rather than a bare number so the cost table stays in one place.
#   1st   magic arrow, create food
#   2nd   harm
#   3rd   fireball
#   4th   lightning, curse, mana drain, greater heal
#   5th   magic reflection
# Energy Bolt has no entry: config__filler_floor below is a higher bar and covers it.
@setvar! config__mana_1st 4
@setvar! config__mana_2nd 6
@setvar! config__mana_3rd 9
@setvar! config__mana_4th 11
@setvar! config__mana_5th 14

# Unholy Symbols banked before each necro ability is allowed to fire. Each figure is the
# ability's own cost plus what the more valuable abilities above it need kept back:
#
#   blood oath        4       its cost, nothing held back, it is the priority
#   corpse skin       4       same bar as Blood Oath, the chain order settles who goes first
#   evil omen         4       same again, so it only ever fires from a walk's surplus
#   poison strike     1       its cost. It only fires while Corpse Skin is up, once the proc
#                             core is spent and behind the filler, so the bank has already
#                             been spent above
#   vampiric embrace  9       3 + 6, walk only, so it competes with nothing else
#
# Symbols arrive one per five seconds and bank to Effective Necromancy / 10, ten here. A
# thirty second cycle regenerates six, and Blood Oath plus Corpse Skin spend exactly six, so
# at Necromancy 100 those two are the sustainable rotation. Raise everything if fights are
# short and walks long, lower if the bank sits full.
@setvar! config__symbols_blood_oath 4
@setvar! config__symbols_corpse_skin 4
@setvar! config__symbols_evil_omen 4
@setvar! config__symbols_poison_strike 1
@setvar! config__symbols_vampiric_embrace 9

# Energy Bolt only fills the gaps between procs, so it stands down before the mana that the
# next opener and the next proc cycle need. 22 for Mana Drain plus Curse, 30 for the four
# proc spells. Below this the core keeps casting and the filler stops.
@setvar! config__filler_floor 52

# How long the two target scoped Grimoire riders last. Curse and Mana Drain both put a two
# minute debuff on the creature, but the +30% damage and +30% mana refund that the script
# actually wants ride for 60 seconds only. The icon outlasts the part worth having, which is
# why this is a timer and not a getlabel.
@setvar! cooldown__magic_window 60000

# Mushroom policy. Create Food T3 returns 25 mana on a 60 second cooldown, and the walk
# between pulls is exactly the window that cooldown needs.
@setvar! config__mushroom_min_count 2
@setvar! config__mushroom_create_mana 70
@setvar! config__mushroom_eat_mana 55

# ####################################################################################
# # WAIT AND COOLDOWN
# ####################################################################################
# Roughly a round trip each. wait__short paces a dclick, wait__long lets a dropped stack
# settle, wait__target is how long a skill cursor gets before the block gives up on it.
# A skill cursor is instant, so that one is only ever spent in full on a failure.
@setvar! wait__short 200
@setvar! wait__long 750
@setvar! wait__target 1000

# How long an ability gets to answer before its reply is read. One round trip plus the
# server's turn, so a little over wait__short. Deliberately not generous: a reply that
# arrives late is not lost, the next pass fires the ability again and reads the cooldown
# refusal instead, which resets the same timer. Too long costs every pass, too short costs
# one extra press now and then.
@setvar! wait__message 400

# Cast polling. A cursor for a spell arrives after the cast time, 0.5 seconds for a first
# circle up to 1.75 for Energy Bolt, and each poll loop leaves the moment the cursor shows.
# The cap is 60 rounds. 25 looked like 2.5 seconds on paper, yet in game on 2026-09-29 a
# fourth circle cursor still came after the loop had ended, so one round here is evidently
# well short of wait__poll. A cursor that turns up after the loop stays open, and every
# block waits on not targetexists, so the whole loop stalls on it. 60 covers a sixth circle
# cast with room. It is a literal on every for line because a for count cannot be a
# variable. wait__cast after the target covers spell recovery, which is 0.2 seconds.
@setvar! wait__poll 100
@setvar! wait__cast 300

# Debounce for repeated warnings. Without it an empty potion bag shouts every pass.
@setvar! cooldown__message 2000

# Heal pacing. heal_action stops the two heal paths from firing back to back,
# greater_heal_retry stops the expensive path from retrying faster than it can land.
@setvar! cooldown__heal_action 1200
@setvar! cooldown__greater_heal_retry 2500
@setvar! cooldown__heal_potion 10000

# Unholy Symbol abilities share one retry window. The game refuses with a cooldown line of
# its own, so this only stops the script asking again every pass while that runs.
@setvar! cooldown__necro_action 30500

# How long Vampiric Embrace waits after "You do not see any corpses near that location."
# Nothing was spent, so it is a short pause while the player walks on, not the window above.
@setvar! cooldown__embrace_miss 5000

# How often the necro hotbar is checked for, and so how long a lost one waits before it is
# opened again. It only closes on a death, a relog or a stray click, and while it is closed
# every ability parks, so up to thirty seconds of that is the price of not looking every pass.
@setvar! cooldown__hotbar_check 30000

# Slow state looked at on a clock rather than every pass (blueprint/razor.html part 6): a plain
# statement costs 5 to 10 ms here and a lookup 20 to 40, so each clock saves the pass one.
#   housekeeping    5 s, one clock for every check that does not need every pass, weight,
#                   instrument recovery, refresh potion and summon names on each tick
#   food           60 s, the buff lasts far longer than that
#   stat potions   10 s, and in a fight only, the buffs last minutes
#   instrument     30 s, it only leaves the backpack on a break or a steal
@setvar! cooldown__housekeeping 5000
@setvar! cooldown__food_check 60000
@setvar! cooldown__potion_check 10000
@setvar! cooldown__instrument_check 30000

# How long DISCO leaves a target alone once its label has shown discord. Discordance runs
# about two minutes, so thirty seconds costs at most that long without it after it lapses.
@setvar! cooldown__disco_seen 30000

# How long PEACE waits before reading the label again once it has shown pacified or a
# barding break. Two seconds is the gap between the 10 second slot and the 12 second
# pacify, so a pacify seen as the slot opens is read again about when it ends.
@setvar! cooldown__peace_seen 2000

# How often the reagent flags are re-read. On this Razor a plain statement costs 5 to 10
# ms and a findtype 20 to 40 (probe, 2026-09-28), so the old read of up to 32 findtype
# on every pass was most of a second per pass. A flag that is stale for half a minute
# costs one refused cast at worst, and the next refresh corrects it.
@setvar! cooldown__regs_refresh 30000

# How long the cache keeps a target that has gone off screen before dropping it.
@setvar! cooldown__target_grace 500

# ####################################################################################
# # STATE
# ####################################################################################
if not varexist var__my_instrument
    @setvar! var__my_instrument 0
endif

if not varexist var__combat_target
    @setvar! var__combat_target 0
endif

# Which song the round robin plays next. 1 discordance, 2 peacemaking, 3 provocation.
# Literal state values, because Razor has no arithmetic to count with.
if not varexist var__song_next
    @setvar! var__song_next 1
endif

# Recomputed once per pass by the target cache. 1 means a live hostile sits inside
# config__target_range. Every later block asks this instead of repeating the find.
if not varexist var__engaged
    @setvar! var__engaged 0
endif

if not varexist var__greater_heal_ready
    @setvar! var__greater_heal_ready 0
endif

# Serial of the summon wearing each lookalike name, 0 while that name is free. Rechecked
# with find every window, so a summon that died or was dismissed frees its name.
if not varexist var__summon_named_1
    @setvar! var__summon_named_1 0
endif

if not varexist var__summon_named_2
    @setvar! var__summon_named_2 0
endif

if not varexist var__summon_named_3
    @setvar! var__summon_named_3 0
endif

# Targets that already carry each half of the opener. Two lists rather than a stage counter,
# so retargeting answers correctly without any per target bookkeeping.
if not listexists 'list__magic_drained_targets'
    createlist 'list__magic_drained_targets'
endif

if not listexists 'list__necro_symbols'
    createlist 'list__necro_symbols'
endif

# The reading the symbol list was last filled from. 99 matches no reading, so the first
# pass always fills the list, whatever a previous run left in it.
@setvar! var__symbols_listed 99

if not listexists 'list__magic_cursed_targets'
    createlist 'list__magic_cursed_targets'
endif

# Serial the last proc spell went at. Poison Strike waits until it is the current target,
# so a mob picked up while the proc bars are still running from the last one is not struck
# before any proc has reached it.
if not varexist var__proc_target
    @setvar! var__proc_target 0
endif

# The target DISCO last saw discorded, 0 when none. Empty at every start.
@setvar! var__disco_seen 0

if not timerexists "timer__blood_oath"
    createtimer "timer__blood_oath"
    settimer "timer__blood_oath" cooldown__necro_action
endif

if not timerexists "timer__vampiric_embrace"
    createtimer "timer__vampiric_embrace"
    settimer "timer__vampiric_embrace" cooldown__necro_action
endif

if not timerexists "timer__corpse_skin"
    createtimer "timer__corpse_skin"
    settimer "timer__corpse_skin" cooldown__necro_action
endif

if not timerexists "timer__evil_omen"
    createtimer "timer__evil_omen"
    settimer "timer__evil_omen" cooldown__necro_action
endif

if not timerexists "timer__embrace_miss"
    createtimer "timer__embrace_miss"
    settimer "timer__embrace_miss" cooldown__embrace_miss
endif

if not timerexists "timer__poison_strike"
    createtimer "timer__poison_strike"
    settimer "timer__poison_strike" cooldown__necro_action
endif

if not timerexists "timer__magic_window"
    createtimer "timer__magic_window"
    settimer "timer__magic_window" cooldown__magic_window
endif

if not timerexists "timer__message"
    createtimer "timer__message"
    settimer "timer__message" cooldown__message
endif

if not timerexists "timer__heal_action"
    createtimer "timer__heal_action"
    settimer "timer__heal_action" cooldown__heal_action
endif

if not timerexists "timer__greater_heal_retry"
    createtimer "timer__greater_heal_retry"
    settimer "timer__greater_heal_retry" cooldown__greater_heal_retry
endif

if not timerexists "timer__target_grace"
    createtimer "timer__target_grace"
    settimer "timer__target_grace" cooldown__target_grace
endif

if not timerexists "timer__hotbar_check"
    createtimer "timer__hotbar_check"
endif

if not timerexists "timer__housekeeping"
    createtimer "timer__housekeeping"
endif

if not timerexists "timer__disco_seen"
    createtimer "timer__disco_seen"
endif

if not timerexists "timer__peace_seen"
    createtimer "timer__peace_seen"
endif

if not timerexists "timer__food_check"
    createtimer "timer__food_check"
endif

if not timerexists "timer__potion_check"
    createtimer "timer__potion_check"
endif

if not timerexists "timer__instrument_check"
    createtimer "timer__instrument_check"
endif

# Expired at every start, like the reagent refresh below, so the first pass looks at all of
# them. The hotbar one is also why there is no separate hotbar setup section above the loop.
settimer "timer__hotbar_check" cooldown__hotbar_check
settimer "timer__housekeeping" cooldown__housekeeping
settimer "timer__food_check" cooldown__food_check
settimer "timer__potion_check" cooldown__potion_check
settimer "timer__instrument_check" cooldown__instrument_check
settimer "timer__peace_seen" cooldown__peace_seen

if not timerexists "timer__regs_refresh"
    createtimer "timer__regs_refresh"
endif

# Expired at every start, whatever a previous run left, so the first pass reads the
# reagents before any block asks for a flag.
settimer "timer__regs_refresh" cooldown__regs_refresh

# ####################################################################################
# # INSTRUMENT
# ####################################################################################
# Only auto detect when the cached instrument is no longer in the backpack, so a pass
# that already holds a good serial costs one find and nothing else.
if not find var__my_instrument backpack
    @setvar! var__my_instrument 0

    if config__use_magic_instrument = 1
        while findtype 3740|3742|3762|3763|10245|20006|20008|20010|20012|20014|20016 backpack as alias__found_magic_instrument
            getlabel alias__found_magic_instrument label__found_magic_instrument

            if "supremely" in label__found_magic_instrument or "exceedingly" in label__found_magic_instrument
                @setvar! var__my_instrument alias__found_magic_instrument
                break
            endif

            @ignore alias__found_magic_instrument
        endwhile

        @clearignore
    elseif findtype 3740|3742|3762|3763|10245|20006|20008|20010|20012|20014|20016 backpack as alias__found_craft_instrument
        @setvar! var__my_instrument alias__found_craft_instrument
    endif
endif

# If auto detect found nothing, ask for a manual pick exactly once. A barding script with
# no instrument has nothing to do, so a failed pick stops rather than limping on.
if not find var__my_instrument backpack
    overhead "[ inst, pick ]" 55
    @setvar! var__my_instrument
    wait wait__long

    if find var__my_instrument backpack as alias__picked_instrument
        getlabel alias__picked_instrument label__picked_instrument

        if "flute" in label__picked_instrument or "drums" in label__picked_instrument or "harp" in label__picked_instrument or "lute" in label__picked_instrument or "tambourine" in label__picked_instrument or "gemshorn" in label__picked_instrument or "hurdy" in label__picked_instrument or "psaltery" in label__picked_instrument or "sackbut" in label__picked_instrument or "shawm" in label__picked_instrument or "vielle" in label__picked_instrument
            overhead "[ inst, {{label__picked_instrument}} ]" 55
        else
            @setvar! var__my_instrument 0
            overhead "[ inst, wrong ]" 33
            stop
        endif
    else
        @setvar! var__my_instrument 0
        overhead "[ inst, out ]" 33
        stop
    endif
endif

# ####################################################################################
# # HERDING
# ####################################################################################
# A double click sets the crook as the active one, and it only has to be in the backpack.
# The wiki gives it no duration, so this runs once here and never in the loop. Setting an
# already active crook again is harmless, which is why there is no "is it already" check.
if config__use_herding = 1
    if findtype "shepherd's crook" backpack as alias__crook
        dclick alias__crook
        wait wait__short
    else
        overhead "[ crook, out ]" 53
    endif
endif

overhead "[ bard necro, on ]" 90

while not dead
    # Let anything already in flight finish before the pass reads state. Both reference
    # files open their loop this way. One while covers both, one statement a pass.
    while queued or casting
        wait wait__short
    endwhile

    # ####################################################################################
    # # SURVIVAL
    # ####################################################################################
    # Paralysis, poison and damage share one test, so a healthy pass pays one statement for
    # the three blocks below instead of three.
    if paralyzed or poisoned or diffhits > config__light_hits
        # ####################################################################################
        # # PARALYZE
        # ####################################################################################
        # First thing in the pass, ahead of every lookup, because it is the one state in which
        # nothing below can act at all. No act window on purpose: paralysed means nothing else is
        # going out anyway, and the pouch is worth spending the pass on the moment it is needed.
        if paralyzed
            if findtype 3705 backpack 38
                yell "[Pouch"
                wait wait__short
            elseif timer "timer__message" >= cooldown__message
                overhead "[ pouch, out ]" 33
                settimer "timer__message" 0
            endif
        endif

        # ####################################################################################
        # # CURE
        # ####################################################################################
        # Ahead of the heal on purpose: a cure is instant and stops the damage that is still
        # coming, a heal spent under poison is partly spent on ticks that have not landed yet.
        # Cure potions have no cooldown, so the spell is only ever the fallback.
        if poisoned
            if not targetexists and not casting
                if findtype "Orange Potion" self
                    hotkey 'Drink Cure'
                    wait wait__short

                    if config__chatty = 1
                        overhead "[ cure pot, on ]" 90
                    endif
                else
                    if timer "timer__message" >= cooldown__message
                        overhead "[ cure pot, out ]" 53
                        settimer "timer__message" 0
                    endif

                    if var__regs_cure = 1 and timer "timer__heal_action" >= cooldown__heal_action and cooldown "walk" = 0
                        hotkey "> Smart Heal/Cure Self"
                        settimer "timer__heal_action" 0
                        wait wait__short

                        for 60
                            if not casting
                                break
                            endif

                            if insysmsg "Your concentration is disturbed, thus ruining thy spell."
                                break
                            endif

                            wait wait__poll
                        endfor

                        if targetexists and diffhits = 0
                            hotkey "Cancel Current Target"
                            wait wait__short
                        endif
                    endif
                endif
            endif
        endif

        # ####################################################################################
        # # HEAL
        # ####################################################################################
        # Light damage takes the cheap agent. Heavy damage drinks first, because the potion is
        # instant, and only falls back to the spell when the potion is on cooldown or gone.
        #
        # The walk guard sits on the two casting lines rather than on the block, because the
        # middle path drinks and drinking while walking is fine.
        #
        # Both agents cast without a cursor, so each waits out casting where it stands and then
        # reads the disturb line itself. That is what keeps a disturbed heal from leaving a stale
        # line for a later cast poll to trip on. The wait is a bounded poll, not a bare while:
        # a disturb drops casting and the poll leaves at once, and if Razor ever left casting
        # stuck the poll still leaves after 2.5 seconds instead of hanging the loop.
        if diffhits > config__light_hits and diffhits < config__emergency_hits and var__regs_heal = 1
            if timer "timer__heal_action" >= cooldown__heal_action
                if not targetexists and not casting and cooldown "walk" = 0
                    hotkey "> Smart Heal/Cure Self"
                    settimer "timer__heal_action" 0
                    wait wait__short

                    for 60
                        if not casting
                            break
                        endif

                        if insysmsg "Your concentration is disturbed, thus ruining thy spell."
                            break
                        endif

                        wait wait__poll
                    endfor

                    if targetexists and diffhits = 0
                        hotkey "Cancel Current Target"
                        wait wait__short
                    endif
                endif
            endif
        elseif diffhits >= config__emergency_hits
            # No interrupt here even though this is the emergency path. By the time this block
            # runs the pass has already drained casting at the top, and every offensive cast
            # finishes inside its own block, so nothing of ours is ever in flight here. The
            # interrupt that matters lives inside each cast's poll loop, where the spell IS in
            # flight and hit points can still be read.
            if not targetexists and not casting
                @setvar! var__greater_heal_ready 0

                if findtype "Yellow Potion" self as alias__heal_potion
                    getlabel alias__heal_potion label__heal_potion

                    if "next usable" in label__heal_potion
                        @setvar! var__greater_heal_ready 1
                    else
                        hotkey 'Drink Heal'
                        cooldown "heal pot" cooldown__heal_potion
                        wait wait__short

                    endif
                else
                    if timer "timer__message" >= cooldown__message
                        overhead "[ heal pot, out ]" 53
                        settimer "timer__message" 0
                    endif

                    @setvar! var__greater_heal_ready 1
                endif
            endif

            if var__greater_heal_ready = 1 and var__regs_greater_heal = 1
                if timer "timer__heal_action" >= cooldown__heal_action and timer "timer__greater_heal_retry" >= cooldown__greater_heal_retry
                    if not targetexists and not casting and cooldown "walk" = 0
                        hotkey "> Greater Heal/Cure Self"
                        settimer "timer__heal_action" 0
                        settimer "timer__greater_heal_retry" 0
                        wait wait__short

                        for 60
                            if not casting
                                break
                            endif

                            if insysmsg "Your concentration is disturbed, thus ruining thy spell."
                                break
                            endif

                            wait wait__poll
                        endfor

                        if targetexists and diffhits = 0
                            hotkey "Cancel Current Target"
                            wait wait__short
                        endif
                    endif
                endif
            endif
        endif
    endif

    # ####################################################################################
    # # COMBAT TARGET CACHE
    # ####################################################################################
    # Songs target the backpack every few seconds, so lasttarget is never safe to act on.
    # This block reads it once a pass, and var__engaged is the answer everything else asks
    # for afterwards. Every targeted cast reads it once more just before delivering, because
    # the script's own target calls overwrite it: a Q pressed between this read and that
    # delivery would otherwise be lost, and the loop would stay on the old mob.
    #
    # The player's pick is taken up anywhere on screen, config__acquire_range, and kept while
    # it stays there, but the loop only engages inside config__target_range. Taking it up only
    # inside that range lost every target the pets opened on from further out: the next song
    # put lasttarget on the backpack and the mob was never seen again (2026-09-29). The range
    # check runs first, so a pass in combat pays the one find it always did, and a pass with
    # no target at all pays none.
    if find lasttarget ground -1 -1 config__acquire_range as alias__fresh_target
        if not dead alias__fresh_target and var__combat_target != alias__fresh_target
            if noto alias__fresh_target = "hostile" or noto alias__fresh_target = "criminal" or noto alias__fresh_target = "enemy" or noto alias__fresh_target = "murderer"
                @setvar! var__combat_target alias__fresh_target
                settimer "timer__target_grace" 0

                if config__chatty = 1
                    overhead "[ target, set ]" 705 var__combat_target
                endif
            endif
        endif
    endif

    @setvar! var__engaged 0

    if var__combat_target = 0
        # no target, nothing to keep
    elseif find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__stored_target
        settimer "timer__target_grace" 0

        if dead alias__stored_target
            @setvar! var__combat_target 0
        elseif noto alias__stored_target != "hostile" and noto alias__stored_target != "criminal" and noto alias__stored_target != "enemy" and noto alias__stored_target != "murderer"
            @setvar! var__combat_target 0
        else
            @setvar! var__engaged 1
        endif
    elseif find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__acquire_range as alias__stored_target
        settimer "timer__target_grace" 0

        if dead alias__stored_target
            @setvar! var__combat_target 0
        endif
    elseif timer "timer__target_grace" >= cooldown__target_grace
        @setvar! var__combat_target 0
    endif

    # ####################################################################################
    # # PASS FLAGS
    # ####################################################################################
    # Derived state, read once so the blocks below compare a flag instead of repeating a
    # lookup. Nothing here acts, so it needs no guard.
    #
    # Reagent graphics, for reading the lines that follow:
    #   3962 black pearl      3972 garlic          3973 ginseng        3974 mandrake root
    #   3976 nightshade       3980 sulfurous ash   3981 spider silk
    # Blood moss is absent on purpose: nothing this script casts uses it.
    #
    # One flag per spell, each carrying that spell's own circle, mana and reagent list.
    #   cure           2nd    6    garlic, ginseng
    #   heal           1st    4    garlic, ginseng, spider silk
    #   greater heal   4th   11    garlic, ginseng, mandrake root, spider silk
    #   create food    1st    4    garlic, ginseng, mandrake root
    #
    #   magic arrow    1st    4    sulfurous ash
    #   harm           2nd    6    nightshade, spider silk
    #   fireball       3rd    9    black pearl
    #   lightning      4th   11    mandrake root, sulfurous ash
    #   curse          4th   11    garlic, nightshade, sulfurous ash
    #   mana drain     4th   11    black pearl, mandrake root, spider silk
    #   energy bolt    6th   20    black pearl, nightshade
    #   reactive armor 1st    4    garlic, spider silk, sulfurous ash
    #   magic reflect  5th   14    garlic, mandrake root, spider silk
    # Read on timer__regs_refresh, not every pass. Each reagent is looked up once, the
    # spell flags are derived from those seven with plain comparisons, and between
    # refreshes the flags simply keep their last value.
    #
    # A cast refused for reagents means a flag is already stale, so that line opens the
    # refresh on its own. Outlands runs the whole cast and refuses only at
    # the target, with no mana spent, so left alone the proc core would spend a full cast on
    # the same spell every pass, and while the stale flag says it is ready Poison Strike and
    # the filler wait as well. The line comes up under the character's own name, seen in
    # game on 2026-09-28.
    if timer "timer__regs_refresh" >= cooldown__regs_refresh or insysmsg "More reagents are needed"
        settimer "timer__regs_refresh" 0

        @setvar! var__has_black_pearl 0
        @setvar! var__has_garlic 0
        @setvar! var__has_ginseng 0
        @setvar! var__has_mandrake 0
        @setvar! var__has_nightshade 0
        @setvar! var__has_ash 0
        @setvar! var__has_silk 0

        if findtype 3962 self
            @setvar! var__has_black_pearl 1
        endif

        if findtype 3972 self
            @setvar! var__has_garlic 1
        endif

        if findtype 3973 self
            @setvar! var__has_ginseng 1
        endif

        if findtype 3974 self
            @setvar! var__has_mandrake 1
        endif

        if findtype 3976 self
            @setvar! var__has_nightshade 1
        endif

        if findtype 3980 self
            @setvar! var__has_ash 1
        endif

        if findtype 3981 self
            @setvar! var__has_silk 1
        endif

        @setvar! var__regs_cure 0
        @setvar! var__regs_heal 0
        @setvar! var__regs_greater_heal 0
        @setvar! var__regs_create_food 0
        @setvar! var__regs_reactive_armor 0
        @setvar! var__regs_magic_reflect 0
        @setvar! var__regs_magic_arrow 0
        @setvar! var__regs_harm 0
        @setvar! var__regs_fireball 0
        @setvar! var__regs_lightning 0
        @setvar! var__regs_curse 0
        @setvar! var__regs_mana_drain 0
        @setvar! var__regs_energy_bolt 0

        if var__has_garlic = 1 and var__has_ginseng = 1
            @setvar! var__regs_cure 1
        endif

        if var__has_garlic = 1 and var__has_ginseng = 1 and var__has_silk = 1
            @setvar! var__regs_heal 1
        endif

        if var__has_garlic = 1 and var__has_ginseng = 1 and var__has_mandrake = 1 and var__has_silk = 1
            @setvar! var__regs_greater_heal 1
        endif

        if var__has_garlic = 1 and var__has_ginseng = 1 and var__has_mandrake = 1
            @setvar! var__regs_create_food 1
        endif

        if var__has_garlic = 1 and var__has_silk = 1 and var__has_ash = 1
            @setvar! var__regs_reactive_armor 1
        endif

        if var__has_garlic = 1 and var__has_mandrake = 1 and var__has_silk = 1
            @setvar! var__regs_magic_reflect 1
        endif

        if var__has_ash = 1
            @setvar! var__regs_magic_arrow 1
        endif

        if var__has_nightshade = 1 and var__has_silk = 1
            @setvar! var__regs_harm 1
        endif

        if var__has_black_pearl = 1
            @setvar! var__regs_fireball 1
        endif

        if var__has_mandrake = 1 and var__has_ash = 1
            @setvar! var__regs_lightning 1
        endif

        if var__has_garlic = 1 and var__has_nightshade = 1 and var__has_ash = 1
            @setvar! var__regs_curse 1
        endif

        if var__has_black_pearl = 1 and var__has_mandrake = 1 and var__has_silk = 1
            @setvar! var__regs_mana_drain 1
        endif

        if var__has_black_pearl = 1 and var__has_nightshade = 1
            @setvar! var__regs_energy_bolt 1
        endif
    endif

    # Unholy Symbols, read off the necro hotbar gump, which prints them as "<have>/<max>".
    # ingump matches a substring, so the chain runs from the top down: "10/" is checked
    # before the single digits, and none of "1/" to "9/" occurs inside "10/10", so each
    # line only ever sees the count it names. Ten is the ceiling: the bank is Effective
    # Necromancy / 10 and this character sits at 100. Should
    # the hotbar ever show more than ten, add the higher readings above the 10/ line, or a
    # two digit reading falls into "1/". A closed gump reads as zero, which parks every
    # ability until the hotbar block reopens it. An elseif chain is evaluated in a single
    # tick, whatever its length.
    #
    # The gates compare against the list, list 'x' >= n being the one size comparison a
    # script variable takes part in. Each reading refills the list only when it differs
    # from the last fill: at ten symbols the old refill on every pass was some twenty
    # statements, this is two, the chain and the inner if. The fill is a literal for
    # count per reading because a for count cannot be a variable.
    if ingump "10/" 622436516
        if var__symbols_listed != 10
            clearlist 'list__necro_symbols'

            for 10
                pushlist 'list__necro_symbols' '1' 'back'
            endfor

            @setvar! var__symbols_listed 10
        endif
    elseif ingump "9/" 622436516
        if var__symbols_listed != 9
            clearlist 'list__necro_symbols'

            for 9
                pushlist 'list__necro_symbols' '1' 'back'
            endfor

            @setvar! var__symbols_listed 9
        endif
    elseif ingump "8/" 622436516
        if var__symbols_listed != 8
            clearlist 'list__necro_symbols'

            for 8
                pushlist 'list__necro_symbols' '1' 'back'
            endfor

            @setvar! var__symbols_listed 8
        endif
    elseif ingump "7/" 622436516
        if var__symbols_listed != 7
            clearlist 'list__necro_symbols'

            for 7
                pushlist 'list__necro_symbols' '1' 'back'
            endfor

            @setvar! var__symbols_listed 7
        endif
    elseif ingump "6/" 622436516
        if var__symbols_listed != 6
            clearlist 'list__necro_symbols'

            for 6
                pushlist 'list__necro_symbols' '1' 'back'
            endfor

            @setvar! var__symbols_listed 6
        endif
    elseif ingump "5/" 622436516
        if var__symbols_listed != 5
            clearlist 'list__necro_symbols'

            for 5
                pushlist 'list__necro_symbols' '1' 'back'
            endfor

            @setvar! var__symbols_listed 5
        endif
    elseif ingump "4/" 622436516
        if var__symbols_listed != 4
            clearlist 'list__necro_symbols'

            for 4
                pushlist 'list__necro_symbols' '1' 'back'
            endfor

            @setvar! var__symbols_listed 4
        endif
    elseif ingump "3/" 622436516
        if var__symbols_listed != 3
            clearlist 'list__necro_symbols'

            for 3
                pushlist 'list__necro_symbols' '1' 'back'
            endfor

            @setvar! var__symbols_listed 3
        endif
    elseif ingump "2/" 622436516
        if var__symbols_listed != 2
            clearlist 'list__necro_symbols'

            for 2
                pushlist 'list__necro_symbols' '1' 'back'
            endfor

            @setvar! var__symbols_listed 2
        endif
    elseif ingump "1/" 622436516
        if var__symbols_listed != 1
            clearlist 'list__necro_symbols'

            for 1
                pushlist 'list__necro_symbols' '1' 'back'
            endfor

            @setvar! var__symbols_listed 1
        endif
    else
        if var__symbols_listed != 0
            clearlist 'list__necro_symbols'
            @setvar! var__symbols_listed 0
        endif
    endif



    # ####################################################################################
    # # HOUSEKEEPING
    # ####################################################################################
    # Checks that do not need every pass share one five second tick, so a pass pays one
    # statement for all of them. Each keeps its own longer clock inside where it has one.
    #
    #   instrument recovery, weight, refresh potion, summon names   every tick
    #   instrument check 30 s, hotbar 30 s, food 60 s, stat potions 10 s (in a fight)
    if timer "timer__housekeeping" >= cooldown__housekeeping
        settimer "timer__housekeeping" 0

        # ####################################################################################
        # # INSTRUMENT RECOVERY
        # ####################################################################################
        # Mid run recovery is auto detect only. A manual pick would block the loop on a cursor
        # the player is not looking at, in the middle of a fight.
        if var__my_instrument = 0
            if not targetexists and not casting
                if findtype 3740|3742|3762|3763|10245|20006|20008|20010|20012|20014|20016 backpack as alias__spare_instrument
                    @setvar! var__my_instrument alias__spare_instrument
                    @setvar! var__instrument_ok 1

                    if config__chatty = 1
                        overhead "[ inst, set ]" 90
                    endif
                elseif timer "timer__message" >= cooldown__message
                    overhead "[ inst, out ]" 33
                    settimer "timer__message" 0
                endif
            endif
        endif

        # ####################################################################################
        # # INSTRUMENT CHECK
        # ####################################################################################
        # Whether the instrument is still in the backpack is looked at every thirty
        # seconds, not every pass. The bard blocks test not warmode, var__instrument_ok and
        # var__my_instrument themselves. A bard block that finds the instrument gone clears
        # var__my_instrument on the spot, which stands them down at once, clock or no clock.
        if timer "timer__instrument_check" >= cooldown__instrument_check
            settimer "timer__instrument_check" 0
            @setvar! var__instrument_ok 0

            if find var__my_instrument backpack
                @setvar! var__instrument_ok 1
            endif
        endif

        # ####################################################################################
        # # OVERWEIGHT
        # ####################################################################################
        # Weight only changes on a pickup, so the housekeeping tick is often enough.
        if not targetexists and not casting
            while weight > maxweight
                if findtype "gold coin" backpack as alias__found_gold
                    lift alias__found_gold config__gold_drop_amount
                    droprelloc 0 0
                    wait wait__short

                    if insysmsg "cannot drop anything"
                        drop backpack -1 -1 -1
                    endif

                    wait wait__long

                    if config__chatty = 1
                        overhead "[ gold, dropped ]" 90
                    endif
                else
                    if timer "timer__message" >= cooldown__message
                        overhead "[ weight, over ]" 53
                        settimer "timer__message" 0
                    endif

                    break
                endif
            endwhile
        endif

        # ####################################################################################
        # # REFRESH POTION
        # ####################################################################################
        # Worth drinking in a fight or out of one, so it stays ahead of the split. The stat
        # potions live under the engaged branch, in STAT POTIONS.
        if stam < 5
            if not targetexists and not casting
                if findtype "Red Potion" backpack
                    hotkey 'Drink Refresh'
                    wait wait__short
                elseif timer "timer__message" >= cooldown__message
                    overhead "[ refresh, out ]" 53
                    settimer "timer__message" 0
                endif
            endif
        endif

        # ####################################################################################
        # # FOOD
        # ####################################################################################
        # Looked at once a minute, the buff lasts far longer. The clock leads, ahead of the
        # findbuff, because skipping that lookup is the point.
        if timer "timer__food_check" >= cooldown__food_check
            settimer "timer__food_check" 0

            if not findbuff 'Food Satisfaction'
                if not targetexists and not casting
                    if findtype tray backpack as alias__found_food
                        dclick alias__found_food
                        wait wait__short
                    endif
                endif
            endif
        endif

        # ####################################################################################
        # # NECRO HOTBAR
        # ####################################################################################
        # The hotbar gump is the source of truth for the Unholy Symbol count the necro stage
        # reads. One block covers both the first open and any later loss, because the timer
        # starts expired. It is looked for every thirty seconds, the clock leading because
        # skipping the gump lookup is the point. The clock only restarts once it has looked,
        # so a missing hotbar behind an open cursor is tried again on the next pass.
        if timer "timer__hotbar_check" >= cooldown__hotbar_check
            if skill "Necromancy" > 0 and not gumpexists 622436516
                if not targetexists and not casting
                    settimer "timer__hotbar_check" 0

                    if findtype 'necromancer book' backpack
                        yell '[necromancyhotbar'
                        waitforgump 622436516 wait__target
                    elseif timer "timer__message" >= cooldown__message
                        overhead "[ necro book, out ]" 33
                        settimer "timer__message" 0
                    endif
                endif
            else
                settimer "timer__hotbar_check" 0
            endif
        endif

        # ####################################################################################
        # # STAT POTIONS
        # ####################################################################################
        # Strength, agility and magic resist, drunk in a fight only so an idle walk does not
        # burn them. The buffs last minutes, so they are looked at every ten seconds, on the
        # housekeeping tick, and the clock only restarts once the act window has let it look.
        if config__use_potion = 1 and var__engaged = 1 and timer "timer__potion_check" >= cooldown__potion_check
            if not targetexists and not casting
                settimer "timer__potion_check" 0

                if not findbuff 'Strength'
                    if findtype "White Potion" backpack
                        hotkey 'Drink Strength'
                        wait wait__short
                    elseif timer "timer__message" >= cooldown__message
                        overhead "[ str, out ]" 53
                        settimer "timer__message" 0
                    endif
                endif

                if not findbuff 'Agility'
                    if findtype "Blue Potion" backpack
                        hotkey 'Drink Agility'
                        wait wait__short
                    elseif timer "timer__message" >= cooldown__message
                        overhead "[ agi, out ]" 53
                        settimer "timer__message" 0
                    endif
                endif

                if not findbuff 'Magic Resist Potion'
                    if findtype "Black Potion" backpack
                        hotkey 'Drink Magic Resist'
                        wait wait__short
                    elseif timer "timer__message" >= cooldown__message
                        overhead "[ resist, out ]" 53
                        settimer "timer__message" 0
                    endif
                endif
            endif
        endif

        # ####################################################################################
        # # SUMMON NAMES
        # ####################################################################################
        # A fresh summon still wears its stock name, "a lich" and so on, and gets the first free
        # lookalike of the character's name. Nothing here casts or opens a cursor, so it runs
        # engaged or not, once per housekeeping tick, one rename per tick: a pair summoned back
        # to back gets its names in the order they appeared.
        #
        # How the pieces hold together. Summons are found by body id. A stock name would find
        # them too, but Razor may keep the old name cached after the rename, and the body never
        # changes. The as alias lives only inside the block that bound it, like every other
        # alias in this file, so the serial is copied into var__fresh_summon before anything
        # reads it: read outside, the alias came back as mobile 4294967295. The client asks the
        # server for every new mobile's status, and that reply is what gives Razor the "this is
        # your pet" flag rename checks, so a summon is known the moment it appears. The noto
        # test started as the old bard-necro follower filter: an own summon reads notoriety 2,
        # friend, in >info, and a wild lich never passes. It also turns away innocent, which is
        # how another player's summon reads unless that player is guild or allied: another
        # player's earth elemental took the third name on 2026-09-29. A renamed summon
        # still matches its body, so the three slot variables carry the serials, a match already
        # sitting in a slot is skipped, and a slot frees itself when find no longer sees its
        # summon alive. The name comes out of the list__summon_names list by slot index: foreach
        # carries a list entry as text, which a variable cannot.
        if config__name_summons = 1 and followers > 0
            if var__summon_named_1 != 0
                if find var__summon_named_1 ground -1 -1 config__summon_range as alias__named_summon
                    if dead alias__named_summon
                        @setvar! var__summon_named_1 0
                    endif
                else
                    @setvar! var__summon_named_1 0
                endif
            endif

            if var__summon_named_2 != 0
                if find var__summon_named_2 ground -1 -1 config__summon_range as alias__named_summon
                    if dead alias__named_summon
                        @setvar! var__summon_named_2 0
                    endif
                else
                    @setvar! var__summon_named_2 0
                endif
            endif

            if var__summon_named_3 != 0
                if find var__summon_named_3 ground -1 -1 config__summon_range as alias__named_summon
                    if dead alias__named_summon
                        @setvar! var__summon_named_3 0
                    endif
                else
                    @setvar! var__summon_named_3 0
                endif
            endif

            @setvar! var__fresh_summon 0

            # Bodies. Lich 24 and ancient mummy 158 read off >info, vampire thrall 722 and rag
            # witch 740 from the old bard-necro follower cache, and the Summon Creature undead pool
            # as far as the stock client art goes, zombie 3, ghost 26, skeleton 50, 56, 57,
            # skeletal knight 147, skeletal mage 148, ghoul 153, rotting corpse 155. Skeletal
            # Fiend, skeletal marksman and rotting flesh are Outlands bodies: read theirs with
            # >info when one is out and add the number here. The plain elementals and daemon a
            # summon gives without Vengeful Spirit, 9 and 13 to 16, are left out: this character
            # always summons through it, and other mages' elementals on screen were being taken
            # for its own, a guildmate's among them, which the noto test cannot tell apart.
            # Walk every match, not just the first: this Razor hands back the same mobile on
            # every call, so a single findtype would return the summon already named and never
            # reach the second one. Each rejected match is ignored for the rest of the walk, the
            # first fresh own summon is copied out, and the ignore list is emptied again so the
            # slot checks above and the rest of the loop see everything.
            while findtype 24|158|722|740|3|26|50|56|57|147|148|153|155 ground -1 -1 config__summon_range as alias__fresh_summon
                if alias__fresh_summon != var__summon_named_1 and alias__fresh_summon != var__summon_named_2 and alias__fresh_summon != var__summon_named_3
                    if not dead alias__fresh_summon and noto alias__fresh_summon != "hostile" and noto alias__fresh_summon != "criminal" and noto alias__fresh_summon != "enemy" and noto alias__fresh_summon != "murderer" and noto alias__fresh_summon != "innocent"
                        @setvar! var__fresh_summon alias__fresh_summon
                        break
                    endif
                endif

                @ignore alias__fresh_summon
            endwhile

            @clearignore

            if var__fresh_summon != 0
                # The first free slot, as an index into list__summon_names. 3 is past the end, so with
                # every name taken the loop below matches nothing.
                if var__summon_named_1 = 0
                    @setvar! var__free_slot 0
                    @setvar! var__summon_named_1 var__fresh_summon
                elseif var__summon_named_2 = 0
                    @setvar! var__free_slot 1
                    @setvar! var__summon_named_2 var__fresh_summon
                elseif var__summon_named_3 = 0
                    @setvar! var__free_slot 2
                    @setvar! var__summon_named_3 var__fresh_summon
                else
                    @setvar! var__free_slot 3
                endif

                foreach summon_name in list__summon_names
                    if index = var__free_slot
                        @rename var__fresh_summon summon_name

                        if config__chatty = 1
                            overhead "[ name, {{summon_name}} ]" 9 var__fresh_summon
                        endif
                    endif
                endfor
            endif
        endif

        # ####################################################################################
        # # DISCO SEEN
        # ####################################################################################
        # Discordance runs about two minutes. Once a target's label has shown it, DISCO
        # leaves that target alone until this forgets it, so a fight does not pay a find
        # and a getlabel on every pass just to learn it is still discorded.
        if timer "timer__disco_seen" >= cooldown__disco_seen
            @setvar! var__disco_seen 0
        endif
    endif

    # ####################################################################################
    # # COMBAT OR WALK
    # ####################################################################################
    # Everything above runs on every pass: the drains, the target cache, the flags and what
    # keeps the character alive, fed and under its weight. Here one test splits the pass. A
    # pass in a fight never looks at the walk blocks and a pass on the walk never looks at the
    # fight blocks, so each pays only for its own gates. Before the split every block asked
    # var__engaged for itself, and a walk pass still stepped through Discordance and
    # Peacemaking down to a failed find each (2026-09-29).
    #
    #   engaged   disco, peace, necro burst, opener, proc core, filler, poison strike
    #   walk      mushroom, self buffs, bard song, vampiric embrace
    #
    # The blocks keep their other conditions, most of them folded onto one line so a pass
    # with nothing to do there pays one statement per block. var__engaged is gone from
    # them, the branch has already answered it.
    if var__engaged = 1
        # ####################################################################################
        # # COMBAT FLAGS
        # ####################################################################################
        # Set by the necro block when an ability lands. Poison Strike checks this and sits out
        # any pass that spent, since the list is only rebuilt on the next pass.
        @setvar! var__symbols_spent 0

        # The Grimoire riders on Curse and Mana Drain run 60 seconds while the debuff icon runs
        # two minutes, so the lists have to expire on a clock rather than on the icon. Sweeping
        # both at once re-opens on a target that was done seconds ago, which costs 22 mana now
        # and then. Per target timestamps would need arithmetic, which Razor does not have.
        if timer "timer__magic_window" >= cooldown__magic_window
            clearlist 'list__magic_drained_targets'
            clearlist 'list__magic_cursed_targets'
            settimer "timer__magic_window" 0
        endif

        # ####################################################################################
        # # DISCO
        # ####################################################################################
        # Discordance runs about two minutes and does not break, so it is applied once per
        # target and then left alone. It goes before Peace because Ensemble wants Discord AND
        # Peace on the same creature, and the one that does not break is worth landing first.
        # bard-mace leads with Peace instead, and for a dexxer that is right: Peace is what stops
        # the mob hitting the player in melee. Here the followers hold the mob and the player is
        # ten tiles back, so the debuff outranks the pacify. Skill is 80 on both, so the odds are
        # the same either way and the order is only about which effect is worth more.
        #
        # Music is shared, so whichever of these two blocks fires first stands the other down
        # until the next pass. That is the arbitration, no extra state needed.
        #
        # warmode is the manual control window, tested on the gate line with the instrument. A
        # target whose label already shows discord is remembered in var__disco_seen and skipped
        # until DISCO SEEN forgets it (housekeeping), instead of a find and a getlabel a pass.
        if var__combat_target != var__disco_seen and cooldown "disco" = 0 and cooldown "music" = 0 and skill "Discordance" > 0 and not warmode and var__instrument_ok = 1 and var__my_instrument != 0 and not targetexists and not casting
            if find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__disco_target
                getlabel alias__disco_target label__disco_target

                if "discord" in label__disco_target
                    @setvar! var__disco_seen var__combat_target
                    settimer "timer__disco_seen" 0
                else
                    useskill 'Discordance'
                    waitfortarget wait__target

                    # Answered once, before the delivery loop. Razor asks for an
                    # instrument only when its cached one is gone, and answering it
                    # makes the skill open the real target cursor, so the wait is
                    # simply repeated. replay is documented as restarting the whole
                    # script from the top, which would re-run the entire setup.
                    if insysmsg "What instrument shall you play"
                        target var__my_instrument
                        waitfortarget wait__target

                        if insysmsg "That is not a musical instrument"
                            @setvar! var__my_instrument 0
                        endif
                    endif

                    if find lasttarget ground -1 -1 config__acquire_range as alias__fresh_target
                        if not dead alias__fresh_target and var__combat_target != alias__fresh_target
                            if noto alias__fresh_target = "hostile" or noto alias__fresh_target = "criminal" or noto alias__fresh_target = "enemy" or noto alias__fresh_target = "murderer"
                                @setvar! var__combat_target alias__fresh_target
                                settimer "timer__target_grace" 0

                                if find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__disco_target
                                    if config__chatty = 1
                                        overhead "[ target, set ]" 705 var__combat_target
                                    endif
                                endif
                            endif
                        endif
                    endif

                    while targetexists
                        if dead alias__disco_target or var__combat_target != alias__disco_target
                            hotkey "Cancel Current Target"
                            wait wait__short
                        else
                            target alias__disco_target
                            wait wait__short
                        endif
                    endwhile

                    wait wait__short
                endif
            endif
        endif

        # ####################################################################################
        # # PEACE
        # ####################################################################################
        # The other half of the Ensemble condition, and unlike Discordance it is short. At
        # difficulty 300 and up the duration formula floors at 15 x Musicianship / 100, which is
        # 12 seconds here, against a 10 second slot cooldown. So it is re-applied continuously
        # rather than once per target: let it lapse and Ensemble and Virtuoso go dark with it.
        #
        # A pacified creature does not attack, and taking damage does NOT break that. Only a
        # barding break does, and while one is running neither Peace nor Provocation can land on
        # that creature, which is why a broken target is left alone until it clears.
        #
        # Either label is then waited out on timer__peace_seen instead of a find and a getlabel
        # on every pass. A barding break runs 40 seconds, so it is read every two seconds
        # rather than on every pass, and Peace lands at most two seconds after it clears.
        if timer "timer__peace_seen" >= cooldown__peace_seen and cooldown "peace/provo" = 0 and cooldown "music" = 0 and skill "Peacemaking" > 0 and not warmode and var__instrument_ok = 1 and var__my_instrument != 0 and not targetexists and not casting
            if find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__peace_target
                getlabel alias__peace_target label__peace_target

                if "pacified" in label__peace_target or "barding break" in label__peace_target
                    settimer "timer__target_grace" 0
                    settimer "timer__peace_seen" 0
                else
                    useskill 'Peacemaking'
                    waitfortarget wait__target

                    # Answered once, before the delivery loop. Razor asks for an
                    # instrument only when its cached one is gone, and answering it
                    # makes the skill open the real target cursor, so the wait is
                    # simply repeated. replay is documented as restarting the whole
                    # script from the top, which would re-run the entire setup.
                    if insysmsg "What instrument shall you play"
                        target var__my_instrument
                        waitfortarget wait__target

                        if insysmsg "That is not a musical instrument"
                            @setvar! var__my_instrument 0
                        endif
                    endif

                    if find lasttarget ground -1 -1 config__acquire_range as alias__fresh_target
                        if not dead alias__fresh_target and var__combat_target != alias__fresh_target
                            if noto alias__fresh_target = "hostile" or noto alias__fresh_target = "criminal" or noto alias__fresh_target = "enemy" or noto alias__fresh_target = "murderer"
                                @setvar! var__combat_target alias__fresh_target
                                settimer "timer__target_grace" 0

                                if find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__peace_target
                                    if config__chatty = 1
                                        overhead "[ target, set ]" 705 var__combat_target
                                    endif
                                endif
                            endif
                        endif
                    endif

                    while targetexists
                        if dead alias__peace_target or var__combat_target != alias__peace_target
                            hotkey "Cancel Current Target"
                            wait wait__short
                        else
                            target alias__peace_target
                            wait wait__short
                        endif
                    endwhile

                    wait wait__short
                endif
            endif
        endif

        # ####################################################################################
        # # NECRO BURST
        # ####################################################################################
        # Each ability goes out through its Razor hotkey, resolves without a cursor, and answers
        # with either "unholy symbols remaining" or the cooldown line, so success is read rather
        # than assumed. The combat three run as one chain in value order, one per pass, so the
        # bank is re-read between them and a lower one never spends what a higher one was saving.
        #
        #   blood oath     +30% follower damage, 5 self damage. The followers are 63% of the
        #                  damage, so this outweighs everything else in this block
        #   corpse skin    every damaging spell adds a disease worth 25% over 30 seconds
        #   evil omen      +20% spell damage, and a 25% chance per spell of half its mana in
        #                  self damage. Below Corpse Skin: smaller bonus with a cost attached
        #
        # Of the rest, Strangle (4) competes with Blood Oath for symbols and delays every hit by
        # five seconds, Wither (5) buys mana only for spells that do no damage, and Pain Spike
        # (5) wants a corpse next to the next mob. None earn a place here.
        #
        # Corpse Skin and Evil Omen only pay off through the loop's own spells, and the loop casts
        # no damage spell while the player is walking or has taken over in warmode. So both wait
        # for a standing player in automatic mode: the first stop after a move opens them together
        # with the procs instead of burning their duration on the walk. Blood Oath feeds the
        # followers, who fight on either way, so it takes neither guard, and the two guards sit on
        # the Corpse Skin and Evil Omen lines instead of on the block. Vampiric Embrace below has
        # no walk guard either: it is walk only, so one would have parked it for good.
        if list 'list__necro_symbols' >= config__symbols_blood_oath and followers > 0 and timer "timer__blood_oath" >= cooldown__necro_action and not targetexists and not casting
            hotkey 'Blood Oath'
            wait wait__message

            if insysmsg "unholy symbols remaining"
                settimer "timer__blood_oath" 0
                @setvar! var__symbols_spent 1

                if config__chatty = 1
                    overhead "[ blood oath ]" 118
                endif
            elseif insysmsg "seconds before you may use that ability again."
                settimer "timer__blood_oath" 0
            endif
        elseif list 'list__necro_symbols' >= config__symbols_corpse_skin and not warmode and timer "timer__corpse_skin" >= cooldown__necro_action and cooldown "walk" = 0 and not targetexists and not casting
            hotkey 'Corpse Skin'
            wait wait__message

            if insysmsg "unholy symbols remaining"
                settimer "timer__corpse_skin" 0
                @setvar! var__symbols_spent 1

                if config__chatty = 1
                    overhead "[ corpse skin ]" 118
                endif
            elseif insysmsg "seconds before you may use that ability again."
                settimer "timer__corpse_skin" 0
            endif
        elseif list 'list__necro_symbols' >= config__symbols_evil_omen and not warmode and timer "timer__evil_omen" >= cooldown__necro_action and cooldown "walk" = 0 and not targetexists and not casting
            hotkey 'Evil Omen'
            wait wait__message

            if insysmsg "unholy symbols remaining"
                settimer "timer__evil_omen" 0
                @setvar! var__symbols_spent 1

                if config__chatty = 1
                    overhead "[ evil omen ]" 118
                endif
            elseif insysmsg "seconds before you may use that ability again."
                settimer "timer__evil_omen" 0
            endif
        endif

        # ####################################################################################
        # # OPENER
        # ####################################################################################
        # Mana Drain then Curse, once per target.
        #
        # Both spells carry a Grimoire rider that is scoped to the creature they were cast on:
        # Curse gives every spell of ours +30% against that target for 60 seconds, Mana Drain
        # gives a 30% refund chance on hostile spells against it. Neither follows to the next
        # mob, which is why membership is tracked per target and not as a global stage.
        #
        # Two lists, so the branch itself is the state. A target that was retargeted mid fight
        # answers correctly with no extra bookkeeping.
        #
        # First, any disturb line nobody read is read off here, so the cursor polls from here to
        # the filler only ever see their own. See Targeted casts at the top.
        if insysmsg "Your concentration is disturbed, thus ruining thy spell."
            # consumed, nothing else to do
        endif

        if not inlist 'list__magic_drained_targets' var__combat_target and var__regs_mana_drain = 1 and mana >= config__mana_4th and not warmode and not targetexists and not casting and cooldown "walk" = 0
            if find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__opener_target
                cast 'Mana Drain'

                for 60
                    if targetexists
                        break
                    endif

                    if insysmsg "Your concentration is disturbed, thus ruining thy spell."
                        break
                    endif

                    if config__interrupt_to_heal = 1 and diffhits >= config__emergency_hits
                        if config__chatty = 1
                            overhead "[ drain, cut ]" 53
                        endif

                        hotkey "> Interrupt"
                        break
                    endif

                    wait wait__poll
                endfor

                if targetexists
                    if find lasttarget ground -1 -1 config__acquire_range as alias__fresh_target
                        if not dead alias__fresh_target and var__combat_target != alias__fresh_target
                            if noto alias__fresh_target = "hostile" or noto alias__fresh_target = "criminal" or noto alias__fresh_target = "enemy" or noto alias__fresh_target = "murderer"
                                @setvar! var__combat_target alias__fresh_target
                                settimer "timer__target_grace" 0

                                if find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__opener_target
                                    if config__chatty = 1
                                        overhead "[ target, set ]" 705 var__combat_target
                                    endif
                                endif
                            endif
                        endif
                    endif

                    if dead alias__opener_target or var__combat_target != alias__opener_target
                        hotkey "Cancel Current Target"
                        wait wait__short
                    else
                        target alias__opener_target
                        wait wait__cast

                        if insysmsg "cannot be seen"
                            # not delivered, so the target stays off the list
                        else
                            pushlist 'list__magic_drained_targets' var__combat_target

                        endif
                    endif
                endif
            endif
        elseif not inlist 'list__magic_cursed_targets' var__combat_target and var__regs_curse = 1 and mana >= config__mana_4th and not warmode and not targetexists and not casting and cooldown "walk" = 0
            if find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__opener_target
                cast 'Curse'

                for 60
                    if targetexists
                        break
                    endif

                    if insysmsg "Your concentration is disturbed, thus ruining thy spell."
                        break
                    endif

                    if config__interrupt_to_heal = 1 and diffhits >= config__emergency_hits
                        if config__chatty = 1
                            overhead "[ curse, cut ]" 53
                        endif

                        hotkey "> Interrupt"
                        break
                    endif

                    wait wait__poll
                endfor

                if targetexists
                    if find lasttarget ground -1 -1 config__acquire_range as alias__fresh_target
                        if not dead alias__fresh_target and var__combat_target != alias__fresh_target
                            if noto alias__fresh_target = "hostile" or noto alias__fresh_target = "criminal" or noto alias__fresh_target = "enemy" or noto alias__fresh_target = "murderer"
                                @setvar! var__combat_target alias__fresh_target
                                settimer "timer__target_grace" 0

                                if find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__opener_target
                                    if config__chatty = 1
                                        overhead "[ target, set ]" 705 var__combat_target
                                    endif
                                endif
                            endif
                        endif
                    endif

                    if dead alias__opener_target or var__combat_target != alias__opener_target
                        hotkey "Cancel Current Target"
                        wait wait__short
                    else
                        target alias__opener_target
                        wait wait__cast

                        if insysmsg "cannot be seen"
                            # not delivered, so the target stays off the list
                        else
                            pushlist 'list__magic_cursed_targets' var__combat_target
                            settimer "timer__magic_window" 0

                        endif
                    endif
                endif
            endif
        endif

        # The rotation waits for Curse, because everything after it is worth 30% more once it
        # has landed. The one thing it does not wait for is a reagent that is not coming back
        # until the next restock: with no Curse reagents the damage goes out without the rider
        # rather than the script standing still in front of a live target.
        #
        # Low mana is deliberately NOT an escape. It regenerates, the followers carry the fight
        # meanwhile, and every point dribbled into an uncursed Magic Arrow is a point the next
        # opener does not have. Waiting for 22 mana and casting with the rider is the better trade.
        if inlist 'list__magic_cursed_targets' var__combat_target
            @setvar! var__opener_done 1
        elseif var__regs_curse = 0
            @setvar! var__opener_done 1
        else
            @setvar! var__opener_done 0
        endif

        # ####################################################################################
        # # PROC CORE
        # ####################################################################################
        # The four Grimoire proc spells. Each carries a large first cast bonus on its own timer,
        # and the game announces when that timer is back, so cooldowns.xml already tracks them
        # and this block simply reads the bars. No timer of our own, which also means the script
        # inherits any cooldown reset the game hands out.
        #
        #   magic arrow  +250% on the first cast in the window
        #   harm         +250%
        #   fireball     +250% as a burn over 15 seconds
        #   lightning    +200% and a hinder
        #
        # Ordered cheapest first. They rarely compete, because a spell whose bar is up is the
        # only one asking, but when two are ready together the cheap one going first keeps more
        # mana available for the opener on the next mob.
        #
        # Each delivery records its mob in var__proc_target, and the flag after this block tells
        # Poison Strike and the filler whether the core is spent. Both wait for it.
        if cooldown "magic arrow" = 0 and var__regs_magic_arrow = 1 and mana >= config__mana_1st and var__opener_done = 1 and not warmode and not targetexists and not casting and cooldown "walk" = 0
            if find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__proc_target
                cast 'Magic Arrow'

                for 60
                    if targetexists
                        break
                    endif

                    if insysmsg "Your concentration is disturbed, thus ruining thy spell."
                        break
                    endif

                    if config__interrupt_to_heal = 1 and diffhits >= config__emergency_hits
                        if config__chatty = 1
                            overhead "[ magic arrow, cut ]" 53
                        endif

                        hotkey "> Interrupt"
                        break
                    endif

                    wait wait__poll
                endfor

                if targetexists
                    if find lasttarget ground -1 -1 config__acquire_range as alias__fresh_target
                        if not dead alias__fresh_target and var__combat_target != alias__fresh_target
                            if noto alias__fresh_target = "hostile" or noto alias__fresh_target = "criminal" or noto alias__fresh_target = "enemy" or noto alias__fresh_target = "murderer"
                                @setvar! var__combat_target alias__fresh_target
                                settimer "timer__target_grace" 0

                                if find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__proc_target
                                    if config__chatty = 1
                                        overhead "[ target, set ]" 705 var__combat_target
                                    endif
                                endif
                            endif
                        endif
                    endif

                    if dead alias__proc_target or var__combat_target != alias__proc_target
                        hotkey "Cancel Current Target"
                        wait wait__short
                    else
                        target alias__proc_target
                        wait wait__cast
                        @setvar! var__proc_target var__combat_target
                    endif
                endif
            endif
        elseif cooldown "harm" = 0 and var__regs_harm = 1 and mana >= config__mana_2nd and var__opener_done = 1 and not warmode and not targetexists and not casting and cooldown "walk" = 0
            if find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__proc_target
                cast 'Harm'

                for 60
                    if targetexists
                        break
                    endif

                    if insysmsg "Your concentration is disturbed, thus ruining thy spell."
                        break
                    endif

                    if config__interrupt_to_heal = 1 and diffhits >= config__emergency_hits
                        if config__chatty = 1
                            overhead "[ harm, cut ]" 53
                        endif

                        hotkey "> Interrupt"
                        break
                    endif

                    wait wait__poll
                endfor

                if targetexists
                    if find lasttarget ground -1 -1 config__acquire_range as alias__fresh_target
                        if not dead alias__fresh_target and var__combat_target != alias__fresh_target
                            if noto alias__fresh_target = "hostile" or noto alias__fresh_target = "criminal" or noto alias__fresh_target = "enemy" or noto alias__fresh_target = "murderer"
                                @setvar! var__combat_target alias__fresh_target
                                settimer "timer__target_grace" 0

                                if find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__proc_target
                                    if config__chatty = 1
                                        overhead "[ target, set ]" 705 var__combat_target
                                    endif
                                endif
                            endif
                        endif
                    endif

                    if dead alias__proc_target or var__combat_target != alias__proc_target
                        hotkey "Cancel Current Target"
                        wait wait__short
                    else
                        target alias__proc_target
                        wait wait__cast
                        @setvar! var__proc_target var__combat_target
                    endif
                endif
            endif
        elseif cooldown "fireball" = 0 and var__regs_fireball = 1 and mana >= config__mana_3rd and var__opener_done = 1 and not warmode and not targetexists and not casting and cooldown "walk" = 0
            if find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__proc_target
                cast 'Fireball'

                for 60
                    if targetexists
                        break
                    endif

                    if insysmsg "Your concentration is disturbed, thus ruining thy spell."
                        break
                    endif

                    if config__interrupt_to_heal = 1 and diffhits >= config__emergency_hits
                        if config__chatty = 1
                            overhead "[ fireball, cut ]" 53
                        endif

                        hotkey "> Interrupt"
                        break
                    endif

                    wait wait__poll
                endfor

                if targetexists
                    if find lasttarget ground -1 -1 config__acquire_range as alias__fresh_target
                        if not dead alias__fresh_target and var__combat_target != alias__fresh_target
                            if noto alias__fresh_target = "hostile" or noto alias__fresh_target = "criminal" or noto alias__fresh_target = "enemy" or noto alias__fresh_target = "murderer"
                                @setvar! var__combat_target alias__fresh_target
                                settimer "timer__target_grace" 0

                                if find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__proc_target
                                    if config__chatty = 1
                                        overhead "[ target, set ]" 705 var__combat_target
                                    endif
                                endif
                            endif
                        endif
                    endif

                    if dead alias__proc_target or var__combat_target != alias__proc_target
                        hotkey "Cancel Current Target"
                        wait wait__short
                    else
                        target alias__proc_target
                        wait wait__cast
                        @setvar! var__proc_target var__combat_target
                    endif
                endif
            endif
        elseif cooldown "lightning" = 0 and var__regs_lightning = 1 and mana >= config__mana_4th and var__opener_done = 1 and not warmode and not targetexists and not casting and cooldown "walk" = 0
            if find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__proc_target
                cast 'Lightning'

                for 60
                    if targetexists
                        break
                    endif

                    if insysmsg "Your concentration is disturbed, thus ruining thy spell."
                        break
                    endif

                    if config__interrupt_to_heal = 1 and diffhits >= config__emergency_hits
                        if config__chatty = 1
                            overhead "[ lightning, cut ]" 53
                        endif

                        hotkey "> Interrupt"
                        break
                    endif

                    wait wait__poll
                endfor

                if targetexists
                    if find lasttarget ground -1 -1 config__acquire_range as alias__fresh_target
                        if not dead alias__fresh_target and var__combat_target != alias__fresh_target
                            if noto alias__fresh_target = "hostile" or noto alias__fresh_target = "criminal" or noto alias__fresh_target = "enemy" or noto alias__fresh_target = "murderer"
                                @setvar! var__combat_target alias__fresh_target
                                settimer "timer__target_grace" 0

                                if find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__proc_target
                                    if config__chatty = 1
                                        overhead "[ target, set ]" 705 var__combat_target
                                    endif
                                endif
                            endif
                        endif
                    endif

                    if dead alias__proc_target or var__combat_target != alias__proc_target
                        hotkey "Cancel Current Target"
                        wait wait__short
                    else
                        target alias__proc_target
                        wait wait__cast
                        @setvar! var__proc_target var__combat_target
                    endif
                endif
            endif
        endif

        # Poison Strike and the filler wait for the whole proc core. Every proc that lands while
        # Corpse Skin is up leaves its disease on the target, so a strike after Magic Arrow alone
        # pops one stack where four were on the way, and a bolt cast while a proc is ready pushes
        # that proc and its next window back by a whole cast.
        #
        # This has to be a flag. A cast does not end the pass, so every block below still gets
        # its turn, which is how both used to go out straight behind Curse and the first proc.
        #
        # 1 once no proc is ready, each one either on its bar or out of reagents. A missing
        # reagent is the same escape the opener takes, it is not coming back until the next
        # restock. Low mana is not, for the reason given at the opener. Read after the proc core
        # has had its turn, so a proc cast this pass already counts. A bar whose message has not
        # arrived yet reads as ready, which only holds both back one pass.
        if cooldown "magic arrow" = 0 and var__regs_magic_arrow = 1
            @setvar! var__procs_done 0
        elseif cooldown "harm" = 0 and var__regs_harm = 1
            @setvar! var__procs_done 0
        elseif cooldown "fireball" = 0 and var__regs_fireball = 1
            @setvar! var__procs_done 0
        elseif cooldown "lightning" = 0 and var__regs_lightning = 1
            @setvar! var__procs_done 0
        else
            @setvar! var__procs_done 1
        endif

        # ####################################################################################
        # # FILLER
        # ####################################################################################
        # The four proc spells spend about 4.3 seconds of a 15 second window and then wait, so
        # roughly two thirds of the window used to go unused. Energy Bolt has no proc timer of
        # its own, and its Grimoire upgrade adds 30% damage and hands back 15 of its 20 mana when
        # the target dies within five seconds, so it is the one spell worth firing purely to fill
        # that gap.
        #
        # Only that gap: var__procs_done keeps it out while any proc is ready, so a bar coming
        # back hands the next cast to the proc core. A bar that returns mid bolt waits out the
        # rest of the cast, 1.95 seconds at most. Poison Strike comes after this block, so a bolt
        # in the same pass adds its disease before the strike pops them.
        #
        # It is also the first thing to stand down when mana runs short, which is what
        # config__filler_floor is for: the opener and one full proc cycle come first.
        if var__procs_done = 1 and mana > config__filler_floor and var__regs_energy_bolt = 1 and var__opener_done = 1 and not warmode and not targetexists and not casting and cooldown "walk" = 0
            if find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__filler_target
                cast 'Energy Bolt'

                for 60
                    if targetexists
                        break
                    endif

                    if insysmsg "Your concentration is disturbed, thus ruining thy spell."
                        break
                    endif

                    if config__interrupt_to_heal = 1 and diffhits >= config__emergency_hits
                        if config__chatty = 1
                            overhead "[ eb, cut ]" 53
                        endif

                        hotkey "> Interrupt"
                        break
                    endif

                    wait wait__poll
                endfor

                if targetexists
                    if find lasttarget ground -1 -1 config__acquire_range as alias__fresh_target
                        if not dead alias__fresh_target and var__combat_target != alias__fresh_target
                            if noto alias__fresh_target = "hostile" or noto alias__fresh_target = "criminal" or noto alias__fresh_target = "enemy" or noto alias__fresh_target = "murderer"
                                @setvar! var__combat_target alias__fresh_target
                                settimer "timer__target_grace" 0

                                if find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__filler_target
                                    if config__chatty = 1
                                        overhead "[ target, set ]" 705 var__combat_target
                                    endif
                                endif
                            endif
                        endif
                    endif

                    if dead alias__filler_target or var__combat_target != alias__filler_target
                        hotkey "Cancel Current Target"
                        wait wait__short
                    else
                        target alias__filler_target
                        wait wait__cast
                    endif
                endif
            endif
        endif

        # ####################################################################################
        # # POISON STRIKE
        # ####################################################################################
        # One symbol to resolve the disease Corpse Skin has been layering on the target: up to
        # eight ticks land at once instead of over the next thirty seconds. On a mob about to die
        # that is damage that would otherwise have gone with it. It sits at the bottom of the
        # symbol ladder and only fires while Corpse Skin is actually up.
        #
        # It goes once the proc core is spent, var__procs_done, and last in the pass, behind the
        # filler. Every damaging spell leaves one disease, so when the pass that spends the core
        # also has the mana for a bolt, the strike pops four procs and a bolt instead of four.
        # Below the filler floor there is no bolt coming, and it pops the four rather than wait.
        # var__proc_target holds it off a mob picked up while the bars are still running from the
        # last one: no proc has reached that mob yet, so the strike waits until the next cycle
        # has gone out there.
        #
        # A target with nothing on it refuses the strike without spending it. Clearing
        # var__proc_target then makes it wait for the next proc to reach that mob, rather than
        # pressing again every pass or sitting out the full window. A cooldown refusal restarts
        # the window, read on both sides of the cursor wait in case it comes back instead of the
        # cursor.
        if timer "timer__poison_strike" >= cooldown__necro_action and var__procs_done = 1 and var__opener_done = 1 and var__proc_target = var__combat_target and var__symbols_spent = 0 and timer "timer__corpse_skin" < cooldown__necro_action and not warmode and list 'list__necro_symbols' >= config__symbols_poison_strike and not targetexists and not casting
            if find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__strike_target
                # A bolt from the filler hits 0.5 seconds after its target and brings
                # its disease then (blueprint/pvp.html part 5). wait__cast covered 0.3 of
                # that and this covers the rest, so on a quick connection the strike
                # does not land ahead of the bolt.
                wait wait__short
                hotkey 'Poison Strike'
                waitfortarget wait__target

                if targetexists
                    if find lasttarget ground -1 -1 config__acquire_range as alias__fresh_target
                        if not dead alias__fresh_target and var__combat_target != alias__fresh_target
                            if noto alias__fresh_target = "hostile" or noto alias__fresh_target = "criminal" or noto alias__fresh_target = "enemy" or noto alias__fresh_target = "murderer"
                                @setvar! var__combat_target alias__fresh_target
                                settimer "timer__target_grace" 0

                                if find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__strike_target
                                    if config__chatty = 1
                                        overhead "[ target, set ]" 705 var__combat_target
                                    endif
                                endif
                            endif
                        endif
                    endif

                    if var__combat_target != alias__strike_target
                        hotkey "Cancel Current Target"
                        wait wait__short
                    else
                        target alias__strike_target
                        wait wait__message

                        if insysmsg "unholy symbols remaining"
                            settimer "timer__poison_strike" 0

                            if config__chatty = 1
                                overhead "[ poison strike ]" 118
                            endif
                        elseif insysmsg "seconds before you may use that ability again."
                            settimer "timer__poison_strike" 0
                        elseif insysmsg "You do not have a poison or disease effect on that target."
                            @setvar! var__proc_target 0
                        endif
                    endif
                elseif insysmsg "seconds before you may use that ability again."
                    settimer "timer__poison_strike" 0
                endif
            endif
        endif
    else
        # ####################################################################################
        # # MUSHROOM
        # ####################################################################################
        # Out of combat only, so the 60 second cooldown burns during the walk rather than during
        # a fight where the cast would compete with the spell rotation. The whole block either
        # eats or casts, so the walk guard rides on the act window line.
        if mana <= config__mushroom_eat_mana and not targetexists and not casting and cooldown "walk" = 0 and not findbuff 'Magic Mushroom Cooldown' and findtype "mushroom" backpack
            hotkey 'Eat Magic Mushroom'
            wait wait__short
        elseif mana >= config__mushroom_create_mana and var__regs_create_food = 1 and not warmode and not targetexists and not casting and cooldown "walk" = 0 and counttype "mushroom" backpack < config__mushroom_min_count
            cast 'Create Food'
            wait wait__short

            for 60
                if not casting
                    break
                endif

                if insysmsg "Your concentration is disturbed, thus ruining thy spell."
                    break
                endif

                wait wait__poll
            endfor
        endif

        # ####################################################################################
        # # SELF BUFFS
        # ####################################################################################
        # Reactive Armor and Magic Reflection stay up until they are used up, so each needs a
        # cast only when findbuff no longer sees it. On the walk only: in a fight the cast would
        # take a slot from the rotation, and what matters is that both are up when the next
        # pull, or a red, arrives. Reactive Armor is 1st circle and goes first, Magic Reflection
        # waits its turn on the next pass. Both are self-only, so no cursor: the same no-cursor
        # shape as Create Food above.
        # The reflect bar is the server's recast lock, 30 seconds after a creature's spell and 60
        # after a player's. It starts on the "Magic reflect removed" line, so the bar is the clock.
        if config__use_reactive_armor = 1 and not findbuff 'Reactive Armor' and var__regs_reactive_armor = 1 and mana >= config__mana_1st and not warmode and not targetexists and not casting and cooldown "walk" = 0
            cast 'Reactive Armor'
            wait wait__short

            for 60
                if not casting
                    break
                endif

                if insysmsg "Your concentration is disturbed, thus ruining thy spell."
                    break
                endif

                wait wait__poll
            endfor
        elseif config__use_magic_reflect = 1 and not findbuff 'Magic Reflection' and cooldown "reflect" = 0 and var__regs_magic_reflect = 1 and mana >= config__mana_5th and not warmode and not targetexists and not casting and cooldown "walk" = 0
            cast 'Magic Reflection'
            wait wait__short

            for 60
                if not casting
                    break
                endif

                if insysmsg "Your concentration is disturbed, thus ruining thy spell."
                    break
                endif

                wait wait__poll
            endfor
        elseif not findbuff 'Spell Siphon' and not findbuff 'Magic Reflection' and var__regs_magic_arrow = 1 and mana >= config__mana_1st and not warmode and not targetexists and not casting and cooldown "walk" = 0
            # Spell Siphon: the first spell to hit us starts a sixty minute buff that shows on the
            # buff bar. A Magic Arrow on self is that hit. Never with Magic Reflection up, the
            # arrow would only bounce off it and burn the reflection. Any disturb line
            # an earlier cast left is read off first, so the poll only sees its own. Before
            # self is targeted, lasttarget is read once more, the way BARD SONG does.
            if insysmsg "Your concentration is disturbed, thus ruining thy spell."
                # consumed, nothing else to do
            endif

            cast 'Magic Arrow'

            for 60
                if targetexists
                    break
                endif

                if insysmsg "Your concentration is disturbed, thus ruining thy spell."
                    break
                endif

                wait wait__poll
            endfor

            if targetexists
                @setvar! var__keep_lasttarget 0

                if find lasttarget ground -1 -1 config__acquire_range as alias__fresh_target
                    if not dead alias__fresh_target and var__combat_target != alias__fresh_target
                        if noto alias__fresh_target = "hostile" or noto alias__fresh_target = "criminal" or noto alias__fresh_target = "enemy" or noto alias__fresh_target = "murderer"
                            @setvar! var__keep_lasttarget 1
                        endif
                    endif
                endif

                if var__keep_lasttarget = 1
                    hotkey "Cancel Current Target"
                    wait wait__short
                else
                    hotkey 'Target Self'
                    wait wait__cast
                endif
            endif
        endif

        # ####################################################################################
        # # BARD SONG
        # ####################################################################################
        # Three 15 minute AoE buffs, each worth 8.5% at this Effective Barding, landing on the
        # player and every follower in range. Sung on the walk between pulls, never in a fight:
        # while engaged, Discordance and Peacemaking keep Music busy so a song rarely gets a
        # window, and playing an instrument interrupts a spell already in flight.
        #
        # Singing on the walk is what removes follower tracking from this script. A resummoned
        # creature picks the songs up on the next walk, so nothing has to notice that it died.
        #
        # findbuff is deliberately NOT the gate. The buffs run 15 minutes, so a findbuff test
        # would be true almost always and the refresh would never fire. The gate is the song
        # cooldown plus the slot each song borrows.
        #
        # A branch only advances var__song_next once the cursor was actually delivered, so a song
        # that could not go out, for any reason, is retried next pass instead of being skipped.
        #
        # The chain only picks the skill and the song after it, the three share the rest. Right
        # before the backpack is targeted, lasttarget is read once more: a hostile the player has
        # just picked would be lost to the backpack, the way a green capper was on 2026-09-29.
        # Then the song stands down, cancels its cursor and leaves lasttarget for the next pass.
        if cooldown "song" = 0 and cooldown "music" = 0 and not warmode and var__instrument_ok = 1 and var__my_instrument != 0 and not targetexists and not casting
            @setvar! var__song_after 0

            if var__song_next = 1 and skill "Discordance" > 0 and cooldown "disco" = 0
                useskill 'Discordance'
                @setvar! var__song_after 2
            elseif var__song_next = 2 and skill "Peacemaking" > 0 and cooldown "peace/provo" = 0
                useskill 'Peacemaking'
                @setvar! var__song_after 3
            elseif var__song_next = 3 and skill "Provocation" > 0 and cooldown "peace/provo" = 0
                useskill 'Provocation'
                @setvar! var__song_after 1
            endif

            if var__song_after != 0
                waitfortarget wait__target

                if insysmsg "What instrument shall you play"
                    target var__my_instrument
                    waitfortarget wait__target

                    if insysmsg "That is not a musical instrument"
                        @setvar! var__my_instrument 0
                    endif
                endif

                if targetexists
                    @setvar! var__keep_lasttarget 0

                    if find lasttarget ground -1 -1 config__acquire_range as alias__fresh_target
                        if not dead alias__fresh_target and var__combat_target != alias__fresh_target
                            if noto alias__fresh_target = "hostile" or noto alias__fresh_target = "criminal" or noto alias__fresh_target = "enemy" or noto alias__fresh_target = "murderer"
                                @setvar! var__keep_lasttarget 1
                            endif
                        endif
                    endif

                    if var__keep_lasttarget = 1
                        hotkey "Cancel Current Target"
                        wait wait__short
                    else
                        target backpack
                        @setvar! var__song_next var__song_after
                    endif
                endif
            endif
        endif

        # ####################################################################################
        # # VAMPIRIC EMBRACE
        # ####################################################################################
        # Vampiric Embrace heals the undead followers off a corpse. Target an enemy or yourself
        # and it searches the surrounding area for one, so the cursor is answered with self. Walk
        # only, when a corpse is what is left of the last pull, and the corpse check keeps it from
        # pressing for nothing. The wiki gives no radius for that search, so a corpse inside the
        # eight tiles looked at here can still be out of reach. That refusal spends nothing, so
        # it only sits out cooldown__embrace_miss.
        #
        # A cooldown refusal restarts the window instead: the script cannot read the game's own
        # cooldown, and the refusal nearly always answers a use whose success line came in late,
        # so a full window from there is about right. It is read on both sides of the cursor
        # wait, in case it comes back instead of the cursor. Before self is targeted, lasttarget
        # is read once more, the way BARD SONG does, so a hostile just picked is not lost.
        if timer "timer__vampiric_embrace" >= cooldown__necro_action and timer "timer__embrace_miss" >= cooldown__embrace_miss and followers > 0 and not warmode and list 'list__necro_symbols' >= config__symbols_vampiric_embrace and not targetexists and not casting
            if findtype 8198 ground -1 -1 8
                hotkey 'Vampiric Embrace'
                waitfortarget wait__target

                if targetexists
                    @setvar! var__keep_lasttarget 0

                    if find lasttarget ground -1 -1 config__acquire_range as alias__fresh_target
                        if not dead alias__fresh_target and var__combat_target != alias__fresh_target
                            if noto alias__fresh_target = "hostile" or noto alias__fresh_target = "criminal" or noto alias__fresh_target = "enemy" or noto alias__fresh_target = "murderer"
                                @setvar! var__keep_lasttarget 1
                            endif
                        endif
                    endif

                    if var__keep_lasttarget = 1
                        hotkey "Cancel Current Target"
                        wait wait__short
                    else
                        hotkey 'Target Self'
                        wait wait__message

                        if insysmsg "unholy symbols remaining"
                            settimer "timer__vampiric_embrace" 0

                            if config__chatty = 1
                                overhead "[ vampiric embrace ]" 118
                            endif
                        elseif insysmsg "seconds before you may use that ability again."
                            settimer "timer__vampiric_embrace" 0
                        elseif insysmsg "You do not see any corpses near that location."
                            settimer "timer__embrace_miss" 0
                        endif
                    endif
                elseif insysmsg "seconds before you may use that ability again."
                    settimer "timer__vampiric_embrace" 0
                endif
            endif
        endif
    endif

endwhile
